                    finalAnswer: "W_{\\text{Earth}} \\approx 118\\,\\mathrm{N}, \\quad W_{\\text{Moon}} = 19.2\\,\\mathrm{N}",
                    explanation: "Mass remains invariant across the universe; weight changes with local gravitational field strength."
